{
  "title": "2D photonic crystal point-defect cavity, E_z eigenfrequency (FDFD)",
  "description": "A square lattice of dielectric rods in air (eps_r 8.9, r = 0.2 a, a = 580 nm: the lattice of the bloch_band_diagram template, whose TM (E_z) band gap spans a / lambda ~0.30-0.44), 11 x 11 rods (5 rings around the centre), with the centre rod replaced by the defect material eps_def (1 = rod removed). The defect pulls a localised monopole resonance into the gap; it leaks only in-plane, through the 5 rings of rods into the CPML, so Q grows roughly exponentially with the number of rings. Solved by the eigenfrequency study (em_fdfd_ez) near a / lambda = 0.38 (mid-gap), with subpixel smoothing on the rod edges. The sweep raises eps_def over 1-4: the monopole moves down through the gap (first run: a / lambda 0.395, 0.378, 0.362, 0.347 with Q 2.6e4, 3.7e4, 4.4e4, 4.6e4; cudss and cudss_mixed agree with each other to 1e-14 in lambda and 1e-10 in Q).\nSize: 40 cells per lattice constant (14.5 nm), ~3.5e5 unknowns. The eigen solver node 'eigen_solver' uses host SuperLU; set its factorization to 'GPU cuDSS' or 'GPU cuDSS, mixed precision' (gpu backend, needs nvmath-python; an LDL^T of the operator scaled by the stretched cell areas) to factor and solve on the GPU, or raise cells_per_a for a larger problem. The monopole is even about both centre lines, so a quarter model (symmetric mirror planes on x_lo / y_lo, the rods cut through the planes) gives the same resonance at a quarter of the unknowns.\nDerived values tab: a_over_lambda_1 (the resonance nearest the target, in units of a / lambda), lambda_1, Q_1 and pml_1 (keep it well below 0.5). No closed-form reference: a demonstration and a solver benchmark.\nField tab: the Snapshot slider steps through the resonances (|E_z| of the monopole concentrated in the defect, decaying through the rings).\nSweep tab: a_over_lambda_1 and Q_1 vs eps_def.",
  "version": 1,
  "parameters": [
    {"name": "a_lat", "expression": "580*nm", "description": "lattice constant (rod spacing)"},
    {"name": "r_rod", "expression": "0.2*a_lat", "description": "rod radius"},
    {"name": "eps_rod", "expression": 8.9, "description": "rod relative permittivity"},
    {"name": "eps_def", "expression": 1.0, "description": "permittivity of the centre (defect) rod; 1 = removed (swept)"},
    {"name": "cells_per_a", "expression": 40.0, "description": "cells per lattice constant"},
    {"name": "dx_cell", "expression": "a_lat/cells_per_a", "description": "uniform cell size"},
    {"name": "margin", "expression": "1*um", "description": "air between the outermost rod cell and the PML"},
    {"name": "L_box", "expression": "2*margin + 11*a_lat", "description": "domain side (11 x 11 lattice cells + margins)"},
    {"name": "c_first", "expression": "margin + a_lat/2", "description": "x (and y) of the first rod centre"},
    {"name": "c_mid", "expression": "c_first + 5*a_lat", "description": "x (and y) of the defect centre"},
    {"name": "f_target", "expression": 0.38, "description": "target normalised frequency a / lambda (mid-gap)"},
    {"name": "lambda_target", "expression": "a_lat/f_target", "description": "eigenfrequency target wavelength (1526 nm)"}
  ],
  "domain": {"size_x": "L_box", "size_y": "L_box"},
  "geometry": [
